WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.234
Scenario: A board dashboard reports only course completion and

2
00:00:03.234 --> 00:00:06.467
total quiz points. Leadership asks whether the programme has

3
00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:09.701
reduced risky behaviour and improved incident readiness. Safest response:

4
00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:12.934
Option A: A balanced measurement set: pre/post knowledge, delayed

5
00:00:12.934 --> 00:00:16.168
retention, novel-scenario decisions, reporting behaviour, qualitative feedback and incident

6
00:00:16.168 --> 00:00:19.401
context, with limitations. A defensible programme uses multiple measures

7
00:00:19.401 --> 00:00:22.994
and avoids claiming that quiz scores alone prove real-world competency.

8
00:00:22.994 --> 00:00:26.228
Option B is unsafe because Completion is an activity

9
00:00:26.228 --> 00:00:30.180
measure and cannot by itself establish behaviour change or risk reduction.

10
00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:33.413
Option C is unsafe because Passing a quiz does

11
00:00:33.413 --> 00:00:36.647
not demonstrate prevention of real attacks or causal impact

12
00:00:36.647 --> 00:00:39.880
on incident rates. Option D is unsafe because A

13
00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:43.114
leaderboard may reflect participation or test-taking and does not

14
00:00:43.114 --> 00:00:46.347
show organizational risk outcomes. In practice: Report baseline and

15
00:00:46.347 --> 00:00:49.940
follow-up measures, delayed retention, scenario transfer, reporting quality and limitations.

16
00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:53.174
Use privacy-preserving aggregation and avoid unsupported causal claims. Key

17
00:00:53.174 --> 00:00:56.407
takeaway: Measure knowledge, retention and observed decisions with context;

18
00:00:56.407 --> 00:00:59.641
do not equate completion or quiz scores with security

19
00:00:59.641 --> 00:01:00.000
outcomes.
